{"agent":"recover-drv","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The Devin descriptor carries `record = \"R-hx-windsurf\"`, but this is the Devin harness (source URLs point at `devin.ai`, file is `.devin/hooks.v1.json`). This change moves the `compat_refs` table to be derived from descriptors (`compat_refs.py` adds `_descriptors`), so a Devin hook/agent is now filed under the Windsurf record. That makes Devin compatibility and record lookups use the wrong harness record, e.g. resolving Windsurf's approval transcript root instead of Devin's whenever a Devin agent descriptor is processed.","digest":"4b34aad6aeae16bb","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/harnesses/devin.toml:46","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/harnesses/devin.toml:46"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"`_dirs` now concatenates the configured `cfg.approvals.transcript_dirs` with every harness descriptor’s `h.transcripts.root`, but it never deduplicates the resulting paths. If the same transcript directory appears in both the user config and a descriptor `[transcripts]` entry—or in multiple overlapping descriptors—`_dirs` returns that directory more than once. Where those duplicate dirs are then globbed into transcript files, the same session's transcript file can be processed twice, causing duplicate approval prompts or decisions for the same transcript.","digest":"996402d19c124547","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:_dirs","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:_dirs"},{"chunk":7,"detail":"The helper’s doc says it accepts a fact table as `dict[str, list[str]]`, but the implementation only takes the list-conversion branch when `get_origin(value_type)` is `tuple`. For a `dict[str, list[str]]` hint, a valid value such as `{\"session\": [\"a.b\"]}` makes `value_type` be `list[str]`, so `get_origin(value_type)` is `list`, the code falls into the table-of-strings branch, and it raises `DescriptorError: <where>: expected a table of strings`. Either the function does not support the documented fact-table shape, or the dataclass/field should be `dict[str, tuple[str, ...]]` and the doc should not imply `list[str]` is accepted.","digest":"a3aeb7059907fabd","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/services/harnessreg.py:_check_table","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/harnessreg.py:_check_table"},{"chunk":8,"detail":"The added line `bad = sorted(set(hk.fields) - HOOK_FIELDS)` assumes `hk.fields` is present and iterable. If a hook descriptor omits the `fields` key — for example, a third-party hook that predates this change, or a `style = \"none\"` hook that does not need fields and was previously valid — `hk.fields` may be `None` or missing, causing `set(hk.fields)` to raise `TypeError`/`AttributeError` instead of a proper `DescriptorError`. This crashes descriptor validation for such inputs. The code should handle missing/`None` fields (e.g., `set(hk.fields or [])`) or reject with a clear error message.","digest":"cf97806d562b0382","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/services/harnessreg.py:302","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/harnessreg.py:302"},{"chunk":9,"detail":"`fieldmap` fills every key absent from a non-empty `[hooks.fields]` table with the corresponding path from `_DEFAULT`:\n`fields.get(name, getattr(_DEFAULT, name))`.\nBut this contradicts the function’s own stated rule that an omitted fact “keeps `FieldMap`'s own default”, and `FieldMap`'s attributes default to `()`. The removed `NORMALIZERS` table relied on that default to mean “ignore this field”: for example, gemini was `FieldMap(prompt=(\"prompt\",), tool=(\"tool_name\",))`. When that entry is moved to a descriptor table containing only `prompt` and `tool`, `fieldmap({\"prompt\": (\"prompt\",), \"tool\": (\"tool_name\",)})` now returns a map with `session=(\"session_id\",\"conversation_id\")` and `model=(\"model\",)` instead of `session=()` and `model=()`. A Gemini hook stdin such as `{\"session_id\":\"sess-1\",\"prompt\":\"hi\"}` then normalizes to `session_id=\"sess-1\"` where the pre-change normalizer produced `\"\"`. The fallback for an omitted field should be `()` (the FieldMap default), not that field’s value in `_DEFAULT`.","digest":"b9e85b8267650cfd","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/services/hookio.py:fieldmap","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/hookio.py:fieldmap"},{"chunk":10,"detail":"Legacy descriptors with the previously valid emitter names are now silently accepted but no longer recognized. For example, a descriptor with `[hooks] emitter = \"claude\"` (old `EMITTERS` key) still passes `plan_for` because `h.hooks.emitter` is truthy, but `emit` does `EMIT_VARIANTS.get(\"claude\", _silent)`, so all hook output becomes silent. `emit_deny` then sees `\"claude\" not in DENY_EMITTERS` and returns `None`, because `DENY_EMITTERS` now contains only `{\"plain\"}`. A PreToolUse hook that used to return a `permissionDecision: deny` for such a descriptor now emits no denial, so a tool can be allowed that should have been blocked.","digest":"4c21f5bf3161225f","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/services/hookio.py EMIT_VARIANTS / DENY_EMITTERS","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/hookio.py EMIT_VARIANTS / DENY_EMITTERS"},{"chunk":12,"detail":"The renamed test claims to verify both field-map and emit-variant resolution but only asserts `plan.emitter in hookio.EMIT_VARIANTS`; the previous normalizer assertion was removed without a corresponding `plan.field_map`/`hookio.FIELDMAPS` check. Given a COMMAND_HOOKED descriptor with a valid emit variant but a dangling `field_map` (for example a typo in the descriptor's `[hooks.fields]` key), the test passes, while `hookio.normalize` will fail at runtime; the ratchet no longer catches this moved-table regression.","digest":"c9b596ba5cfaddc5","family":"deepseek","location":"tests/test_harness_conformance.py:test_the_field_map_and_emit_variant_resolve","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_harness_conformance.py:test_the_field_map_and_emit_variant_resolve"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"A partial `[hooks.fields]` table does not keep `FieldMap`'s own defaults, despite the docstring. `tool` on `FieldMap` defaults to `()`, while `_DEFAULT.tool` is `(\"tool_name\",)`. Given `fields={\"session\": (\"conversation_id\", \"session_id\"), \"prompt\": (\"prompt\",), \"source\": (), \"model\": (\"model\",), \"cwd\": (\"workspace_roots.0\",)}` (the old Cursor map, which never set `tool`), `fieldmap` fills `tool` from `_DEFAULT`. `normalize` then treats stdin `{\"tool_name\": \"Shell\"}` as a tool hook; the previous dialect left `tool` empty and would not.","digest":"9cd69e6f5f168e2d","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/hookio.py:fieldmap","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/hookio.py:fieldmap"}],"chunks_total":5,"coverage":"5/5 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":52252,"diff_sha":"63e0bcb44153cc6fa67449cae698243eed09a0de186d606175f3eaffe43434e6","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":2.0,"excluded_bytes":403,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["ddflow/templates/default.toml"],"family":"deepseek","findings":8,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"5fa2765ee203d9d3","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DRV-migrate.rubber_duck.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261108T000404Z-623bc5d3.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794095389.557749,"family":"moonshot","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"kimi-for-coding-highspeed","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"kimi-k3"}],"review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5],"reviewed_head":"c93561082153f11b1d318d280bb33b885d8b5969","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/harness.py":"100644 deefd12c4433d5e772032251b8d2a6327efb5ad2","ddflow/config_sections/approvals.py":"100644 643dfb42b920aae4b570f82f7e990949e26996cb","ddflow/harnesses/antigravity.toml":"100644 5001c30bf66dd50d2583921a5bb7b3aed38250cc","ddflow/harnesses/claude.toml":"100644 0e8942879b1a385dfca1884404e3eb68a9193d5c","ddflow/harnesses/cline.toml":"100644 cf2e9cbd40e2343606670b1d76680aa1c11dc6f4","ddflow/harnesses/codex.toml":"100644 1f2e01a750906120e2786c3e4355a0509a512f05","ddflow/harnesses/copilot.toml":"100644 3cce7cd977a63f6b9fc14cada41a2721b2a5bb7a","ddflow/harnesses/cursor.toml":"100644 615e3b824b9e86f0c81e8f15ac311a8d2eec97d9","ddflow/harnesses/devin.toml":"100644 a044fcc2fc564bba3d032a5d5f1fdc197397d295","ddflow/harnesses/dsh.toml":"100644 b4724579cf0f31cfec5aa241a284309d5421b7de","ddflow/harnesses/gemini.toml":"100644 db0d6a350bd2ba0c64732d141b047283348542ac","ddflow/harnesses/goose.toml":"100644 216e8b0607a8b369148b681ef81921edf40a2066","ddflow/harnesses/grok.toml":"100644 3b6865884093d36d2916dfd5898d634df5570c50","ddflow/harnesses/kilo.toml":"100644 c6823da8eb5a23aa8c6890a2b6b07b2bbb9c959e","ddflow/harnesses/kimi.toml":"100644 239a36cdc221dea91c7cb30d5421967d736480f4","ddflow/harnesses/opencode.toml":"100644 177828b4e6f518796c92a246a056f1904ee8a7d3","ddflow/harnesses/openhands.toml":"100644 49caf21b76482965fe430bec04eca84cc65aab21","ddflow/harnesses/qwen.toml":"100644 de267643be254b4e16d76357482680fad8bb7e95","ddflow/harnesses/tabnine.toml":"100644 7d3aa72131f5fd4c84782c243edd0c464adc98da","ddflow/harnesses/vscode.toml":"100644 6c54b09e9f246e3b5830eab3073b58867e92ba61","ddflow/harnesses/windsurf.toml":"100644 20b310e01667abdb3579b65258f670469641f036","ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py":"100644 90a4d68382b6657ad49b4fe8d9179631e76c3baa","ddflow/services/compat_refs.py":"100644 2acf559dd02bb053b55c82628fb520b94e84110f","ddflow/services/engines/emit.py":"100644 744c40b3d671f4358a25f59a72c81e957fe07b67","ddflow/services/harnessreg.py":"100644 2b22afcaf85fb3c2ea160978084bab4fe4a2a168","ddflow/services/hookio.py":"100644 80e6085508564f2816397df23a12dc3f343a37e1","ddflow/templates/default.toml":"100644 71367e486a2b353c25b23bdac7e441b7be8cbcd4","tests/harness_conformance/report.py":"100644 8571ccf1c114cf474782e02532d38cbca21ad27d","tests/test_dsh_descriptor.py":"100644 0e1c5b1b72bb7948e30123d15223d0d7a93938b1","tests/test_engines.py":"100644 83c8c237d0c4ec10b3285873119c6ebd28194a61","tests/test_harness_conformance.py":"100644 35189d12aad942098a5fd53164fb00566ab25217","tests/test_hook_core.py":"100644 17028d1760d13c482a4a3577b6fe80efc9f523f9","tests/test_no_agent_literals.py":"100644 acefcfaf0b556f72f2f9ce6f043b0e51c6f8e17c"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","reviewer_families":["deepseek","google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/harnesses/devin.toml:46","ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:_dirs","ddflow/services/harnessreg.py:_check_table","ddflow/services/harnessreg.py:302","ddflow/services/hookio.py:fieldmap","ddflow/services/hookio.py EMIT_VARIANTS / DENY_EMITTERS","tests/test_harness_conformance.py:test_the_field_map_and_emit_variant_resolve","ddflow/services/hookio.py:fieldmap"],"tree_sha":"c93561082153+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"8 finding(s)"},"id":"ea04065e66b977dd6461d915f","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":151094,"schema":1,"subject":"DRV-migrate","ts":"2026-11-08T00:06:08.332951Z"}
