{"agent":"recover-drv","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`devin.toml` declares `record = \"R-hx-windsurf\"` even though the file is the Devin harness descriptor (`sources` points to `docs.devin.ai`). If descriptors are indexed by `record`, this Devin descriptor will collide with `windsurf.toml`’s `R-hx-windsurf`, so one of the two harnesses is overwritten or rejected as duplicate. The record id here is wrong and should identify the Devin record, not the Windsurf record.","digest":"d6610b4c7cd24313","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/harnesses/devin.toml:46","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/harnesses/devin.toml:46"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"`roots.extend(h.transcripts.root)` is called on the descriptor's `[transcripts] root` value, which is a single transcript-root path string. `list.extend` on a string appends each character. Given a descriptor with `[transcripts] root = \"/tmp/agent-run\"`, `_dirs` returns paths like `/`, `t`, `m`, `p`, `/`, `a`, ... and approvals never scans the real transcript directory. It should be `roots.append(h.transcripts.root)` (or otherwise treat `root` as a one-element list).","digest":"83bfc4406ed5e166","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:184","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:184"},{"chunk":8,"detail":"The command-hook-style requirement was changed from `(hk.normalizer and hk.emitter and hk.file)` to `(hk.emitter and hk.file)`, so a descriptor with a command hook style, a `file`, an `emitter`, and no `[hooks.fields]` now passes validation. Since this change moves NORMALIZERS into `[hooks.fields]` (the same `hk.fields` this validator now checks only for unknown keys, not presence), the invalid descriptor reaches the normalizer/emit path without the required normalizer data; previously `_validate_hook` rejected it up front with `DescriptorError`.","digest":"e1f1ec944abbdb83","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/services/harnessreg.py:_validate_hook","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/harnessreg.py:_validate_hook"},{"chunk":9,"detail":"`fieldmap` fills missing keys from `_DEFAULT` via `fields.get(name, getattr(_DEFAULT, name))`, but the function’s own contract says a field omitted from a non-empty `[hooks.fields]` table keeps `FieldMap`’s own default. That default is the empty tuple, not the Claude dialect. Concrete input: `fields={\"prompt\": (\"prompt\",), \"tool\": (\"tool_name\",)}` (the old Gemini map) produces a `FieldMap` with `session=(\"session_id\",\"conversation_id\")` and `model=(\"model\",)`. For stdin `{\"prompt\":\"hi\",\"tool_name\":\"t\",\"session_id\":\"sid\",\"model\":\"m\"}`, `normalize` now extracts `session_id=\"sid\"` and `model=\"m\"`, whereas the pre-change `NORMALIZERS[\"gemini\"]` ignored both. Any descriptor that legitimately omits a non-Claude field inherits Claude session/model extraction and can corrupt normalized hooks.","digest":"ffc2946ce2e227fc","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/services/hookio.py:fieldmap","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/hookio.py:fieldmap"},{"chunk":12,"detail":"The renamed test is supposed to verify both the field map and the emit variant resolve, but it only asserts `plan.emitter in hookio.EMIT_VARIANTS`. The field map / normalizer half is never checked. A command hook descriptor whose `plan_for` result has a missing or unknown field map, or no `field_map` attribute at all, will still pass as long as its emitter is known, so the conformance ratchet no longer catches broken `[hooks.fields]` data.","digest":"da1fe27a11163ed0","family":"deepseek","location":"tests/test_harness_conformance.py:test_the_field_map_and_emit_variant_resolve","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_harness_conformance.py:test_the_field_map_and_emit_variant_resolve"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"A non-empty `[hooks.fields]` table that omits a fact does not keep `FieldMap`'s own default, despite the docstring. `fieldmap({\"session\": (\"trajectory_id\",)})` fills every other name from `_DEFAULT` (Claude), so `prompt` becomes `(\"prompt\",)` and `tool` becomes `(\"tool_name\",)`. `normalize` then reads those paths. A payload whose real prompt is only `tool_info.user_prompt` (old cascade) and that also has an unrelated top-level `prompt` is therefore taken from the wrong field. Omitting a key cannot mean \"this dialect has no path\"; only an explicit empty tuple can, and `normalize` does not apply the Claude fallback its own docstring claims for an empty `FieldMap` either.","digest":"02250a9e0463ecc1","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/hookio.py:fieldmap","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/hookio.py:fieldmap"}],"chunks_total":5,"coverage":"5/5 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":52252,"diff_sha":"63e0bcb44153cc6fa67449cae698243eed09a0de186d606175f3eaffe43434e6","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1.5,"excluded_bytes":403,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["ddflow/templates/default.toml"],"family":"deepseek","findings":6,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"0fd1be8b0d06e824","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DRV-migrate.critic.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261108T002151Z-2877b2db.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794096375.7342575,"family":"moonshot","gate":"critic","model":"kimi-for-coding-highspeed","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"kimi-k3"}],"review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5],"reviewed_head":"c93561082153f11b1d318d280bb33b885d8b5969","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/harness.py":"100644 deefd12c4433d5e772032251b8d2a6327efb5ad2","ddflow/config_sections/approvals.py":"100644 643dfb42b920aae4b570f82f7e990949e26996cb","ddflow/harnesses/antigravity.toml":"100644 5001c30bf66dd50d2583921a5bb7b3aed38250cc","ddflow/harnesses/claude.toml":"100644 0e8942879b1a385dfca1884404e3eb68a9193d5c","ddflow/harnesses/cline.toml":"100644 cf2e9cbd40e2343606670b1d76680aa1c11dc6f4","ddflow/harnesses/codex.toml":"100644 1f2e01a750906120e2786c3e4355a0509a512f05","ddflow/harnesses/copilot.toml":"100644 3cce7cd977a63f6b9fc14cada41a2721b2a5bb7a","ddflow/harnesses/cursor.toml":"100644 615e3b824b9e86f0c81e8f15ac311a8d2eec97d9","ddflow/harnesses/devin.toml":"100644 a044fcc2fc564bba3d032a5d5f1fdc197397d295","ddflow/harnesses/dsh.toml":"100644 b4724579cf0f31cfec5aa241a284309d5421b7de","ddflow/harnesses/gemini.toml":"100644 db0d6a350bd2ba0c64732d141b047283348542ac","ddflow/harnesses/goose.toml":"100644 216e8b0607a8b369148b681ef81921edf40a2066","ddflow/harnesses/grok.toml":"100644 3b6865884093d36d2916dfd5898d634df5570c50","ddflow/harnesses/kilo.toml":"100644 c6823da8eb5a23aa8c6890a2b6b07b2bbb9c959e","ddflow/harnesses/kimi.toml":"100644 239a36cdc221dea91c7cb30d5421967d736480f4","ddflow/harnesses/opencode.toml":"100644 177828b4e6f518796c92a246a056f1904ee8a7d3","ddflow/harnesses/openhands.toml":"100644 49caf21b76482965fe430bec04eca84cc65aab21","ddflow/harnesses/qwen.toml":"100644 de267643be254b4e16d76357482680fad8bb7e95","ddflow/harnesses/tabnine.toml":"100644 7d3aa72131f5fd4c84782c243edd0c464adc98da","ddflow/harnesses/vscode.toml":"100644 6c54b09e9f246e3b5830eab3073b58867e92ba61","ddflow/harnesses/windsurf.toml":"100644 20b310e01667abdb3579b65258f670469641f036","ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py":"100644 90a4d68382b6657ad49b4fe8d9179631e76c3baa","ddflow/services/compat_refs.py":"100644 2acf559dd02bb053b55c82628fb520b94e84110f","ddflow/services/engines/emit.py":"100644 744c40b3d671f4358a25f59a72c81e957fe07b67","ddflow/services/harnessreg.py":"100644 2b22afcaf85fb3c2ea160978084bab4fe4a2a168","ddflow/services/hookio.py":"100644 80e6085508564f2816397df23a12dc3f343a37e1","ddflow/templates/default.toml":"100644 71367e486a2b353c25b23bdac7e441b7be8cbcd4","tests/harness_conformance/report.py":"100644 8571ccf1c114cf474782e02532d38cbca21ad27d","tests/test_dsh_descriptor.py":"100644 0e1c5b1b72bb7948e30123d15223d0d7a93938b1","tests/test_engines.py":"100644 83c8c237d0c4ec10b3285873119c6ebd28194a61","tests/test_harness_conformance.py":"100644 35189d12aad942098a5fd53164fb00566ab25217","tests/test_hook_core.py":"100644 17028d1760d13c482a4a3577b6fe80efc9f523f9","tests/test_no_agent_literals.py":"100644 acefcfaf0b556f72f2f9ce6f043b0e51c6f8e17c"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","reviewer_families":["deepseek","google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/harnesses/devin.toml:46","ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:184","ddflow/services/harnessreg.py:_validate_hook","ddflow/services/hookio.py:fieldmap","tests/test_harness_conformance.py:test_the_field_map_and_emit_variant_resolve","ddflow/services/hookio.py:fieldmap"],"tree_sha":"c93561082153+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"6 finding(s)"},"id":"e24c640a19e60c5a681d8295d","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":151145,"schema":1,"subject":"DRV-migrate","ts":"2026-11-08T00:24:50.362729Z"}
